plaso.tsv.gz: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from the logs in tests/fixtures/plaso/, with the parsers winpca_dic,
winpca_db0, text/winiis, text/winfirewall, text/powershell_transcript,
text/teamviewer_*, text/setupapi and text/sccm (psort -o json_line), one line
per distinct event: its kind, file, wall-clock time (to the millisecond) and
the fields compared. Written from plaso's output, not from this crate.

SCCM entries are compared without their times: plaso applies the log's time
zone bias inconsistently (a +480 entry kept as UTC, a -330 entry shifted the
other way); this crate reads the bias as Windows defines it, UTC = local time
+ bias, and its unit test checks that.

wer.tsv: the reports of tests/fixtures/written/wer/ read with Python's own
codecs (gen_wer.py).

screenconnect.tsv: the ScreenConnect samples of
tests/fixtures/written/screenconnect/ read with Python's own sqlite3,
xml.etree and urllib.parse (gen_screenconnect.py); the deleted events to
recover are listed by the generator itself (deleted.tsv there).
